{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473046-kimetsu-no-yaiba-as-a-wyld-hunt-story-aka-demon-slayer-as-immaculate-propaganda","id":1473046,"title":"Kimetsu No Yaiba as a Wyld Hunt Story, aka \"Demon Slayer as Immaculate propaganda\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-22T15:10:50-08:00","id":1473046,"title":"Kimetsu No Yaiba as a Wyld Hunt Story, aka \"Demon Slayer as Immaculate propaganda\"","content":"<br /> So!<br /> <br /> I'm hardly the first person on this forum to make this comparison, but there's plenty of similarities between the plot of &quot;<i>Demon Slayer: Kimetsu No Yaiba</i>&quot; manga by Koyoharu Gotouge and Dragonblood-led Wyld Hunts in the world of <i>Exalted</i>! Wandering demon hunters who practical elemental martial arts, shapeshifting demons symbolically linked to the moon, quasi-Buddhist themes of reincarnations and past-life memories, etc.<br /> <br /> The parallels aren't perfect, of course. &quot;Anathema&quot; aren't weak to the sun, invulnerable to mortal weapons, or able to create more of themselves with their corrupted blood, and &quot;Demons&quot; aren't semi-divine heroes granted power by the Sun, Moon, or the sovereigns of Death and Hell. Still, I think it'd be fun to try importing characters from &quot;Kimetsu No Yaiba&quot; into the Third Age of Creation and see how their fates would change in a world where Exalted are a thing!<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> _______________________<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kamado Tanjiro</b> would probably be an <b>Exigent \u2013</b> specifically the Chosen of &quot;Hinokami, God of Fire And Charcoal.&quot; After his clan of charcoal burners is slaughtered by a passing Anathema and his only sister becomes one of the &quot;Moon-Mad,&quot; Tanjiro joins a local band of <i>Shikari</i> who call themselves the &quot;Demon Slayer Corps,&quot; seeking the strength to kill the ancient Anathema called Kibutsuji Muzan and somehow restore Nezuko's humanity. Start out with Brawling Charms flavored to revolve around head-butts, learns Water Dragon Style, and finally switches to a Martial Arts Style more suited to the fire-and-coal theme of his Exigence. Unlike in canon Kimetsu no Yaiba, though, his understanding of &quot;humanity&quot; and &quot;demonhood&quot; is tragically askew due to being raised in a culture dominated by the Immaculate Faith...<br /> <br /> <b>Kamado Nezuko</b>, I suspect, would be a <b>Castless Lunar</b>, chosen by Luna as she struggled to survive her wounds and reach her dying family members. I could probably home-brew some reason why she has the muteness and amnesia of her canon demonic self...but I think it would be more interesting to give her Exalted incarnation the sunny, optimistic and kind personality of her canon-human self (and beneath that cheer, a primal rage towards injustice and a sorrowful belief that one day Tanjiro will need to put her down). She'd have a vast amount of Charms related to resisting/recovering from damage, could perhaps shapeshift into cows, goats, chickens, deer and other animals that get regularly eaten by humans anyways. As for her Totem and Tell...Bunny ears, perhaps?<br /> <br /> <b>Agatsuma Zenitsu</b> would almost certainly be an <b>Air Aspect</b> and <b>Outcaste</b>, his backstory and character growth more or less unchanged from the manga. Spams Single Point Shining Into The Void Martial Arts Charms during combat, further enhanced with Dragonblood Charms that enhance his speed. <br /> <br /> <b>Hashibira Inosuke</b> would also need few changes to his backstory...although in the world of Exalted, he might have been raised by and Chosen to be the <b>Exigent</b> of a family of sentient Boar Gods, <i>Princess Mononoke</i>-style. Naturally, his boar mask and contortionist abilities would cause strangers to regularly mistake him for a Lunar Anathema.<br /> <br /> <b>Tsuyuri Kanao</b> would probably be a <b>Wood Aspect</b> whose Exaltation freed her from a life of slavery, though the mental scars from her life of subjugation are harder to shake off. Aside from knowing Wood Dragon Style, she probably has a wide number of Awareness charms that improve her acuity and danger sense during battle.<br /> <br /> In canon, <b>Shinazugawa Genya</b> was unable to master the principles of Breathing Techniques, so his Exalted incarnation would probably be the one <b>Mortal</b> amongst a group of Exigents and Dragonbloods. Just like in canon, he'd surpass his mortal limits by devouring the flesh of supernatural beings in order to heal himself and gain temporary combat Mutations (an ability granted by God-Blooded heritage, borderline heretical sorcery, or something even odder). Naturally, he'd wield a sword and flame piece in battle, and yearn desperately to mend fences with his Air Aspect <i>Shikari</i> brother.<br /> <br /> ___________________<br /> <br /> <br /> Those are my takes on the &quot;Final Selection&quot; group of <i>Demon Slayer</i> protagonists and how they might be translated to the Exalted setting...but how would you, the readers of this post, &quot;Exalt-tify&quot; the cast of <i>Kimetsu No Yaiba</i>? <br /> <br /> Would the Demon Slayer Corps and their Hashira elites be a formal branch of the Immaculate Faith? Would Muzan and his Demons become a Deathlord and his retinue of Abyssals, or a faction of Lunars who went deep off the reservation? Would the &quot;good vs. evil&quot; plot of <i>Kimetsu No Yaiba </i>break down in the face of a world where not every &quot;Anathema&quot; is evil, or would the protagonists break away from the Immaculate worldview to follow their own path of heroism?<br /> <br /> Would love to hear your thoughts!<br /> <br /> %%%<br /> <br /> So!<br /> <br /> There are many similarities between the plot of &quot;<i>Demon Slayer: Kimetsu No Yaiba</i>&quot; manga by Koyoharu Gotouge and the Dragonblood-led Wyld Hunts in the world of